# `rtk vitest run` writes its report here; a parse failure leaves it behind
.vitest/
# oxlint resolves `overrides[].files` relative to its config, so the toolchain contract test must write its fixture
# config at the repository root. It is removed in `afterAll`, but a concurrent or interrupted run would otherwise dirty
# `git status` and block the release precheck.
.oxlintrc.contract-*.json
.cache/
.records/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
.DS_Store
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Credential shapes. Nothing in this repository needs any of these tracked, and a public repository
# makes an accidental commit unrecoverable: a force-push removes it from the branch but not from the
# forks, caches, and mirrors that already read it. Deny them by pattern so the mistake cannot happen
# in the first place, rather than relying on review to catch it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
id_ecdsa
.npmrc
